<title>UK: Bulker due to load grain for Saudi under repair.</title>
<headline>Bulker due to load grain for Saudi under repair.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cyprus-flag bulk carrier Sofron, due to load grain consigned for Saudi Arabia in the next few weeks, is at Prince Rupert for repairs, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said.</p>
<p>The 68,024 dwt vessel dragged its anchor and grounded temporarily, causing shell plating damage.</p>
<p>Repairs are underway at the port in British Colombia, Canada, to enable the vessel to proceed.</p>
<p>Sofron arrived at Prince Rupert around January 14. Lloyds did not say how long repairs were likely to take.</p>
</text>
